Answer: Variable shadowing occurs when constructor parameters have the same names as instance variables.

```java
class Demo {
int a;
int b;
```

Demo(int a, int b) {

```java
this.a = a;
this.b = b;
}
}
```

Answer: The this keyword refers to the current object's instance variable.

```java
this.a = a;
this.b = b;
```

The left side refers to the instance variables, while the right side refers to the constructor parameters.

