Answer: The child constructor can call the parent constructor using super(...).

```java
class Demo {
int a;
int b;
```

Demo(int a, int b) {

```java
this.a = a;
this.b = b;
}
}
class Demo1 extends Demo {
int c;
int d;
```

Demo1(int c, int d) {

```java
super(10, 20);
this.c = c;
this.d = d;
}
}
```

Here, super(10, 20) invokes the parameterized constructor of Demo.

